# Optional API Gateway base URL after a backend deployment, for example:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://example.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/dev
# Explicitly opt individual modules into the authenticated API. Leave both unset
# to preserve local demo mode.
# VITE_DEVELOPER_PASSPORT_MODE=api
# VITE_PROJECT_COLLABORATION_MODE=api
# Cognito configuration enables sign-in, registration, verification and password reset.
# For local development, put these three values in the ignored .env.development.local.
# Source them from the deployed SAM outputs CognitoRegion, UserPoolId and UserPoolClientId.
# Amplify builds receive the same names from the branch's Environment variables settings.
# These are public identifiers; never put a client secret, AWS key, or token here.
# VITE_COGNITO_REGION=
# VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=
# VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_CLIENT_ID=
# These are the six supported VITE variables: API URL, two API-mode switches,
# and the three Cognito identifiers above.
# Never place credentials, Cognito secrets, or private tokens in this file.
